text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', "As Phyrexian Revoker enters the battlefield, choose a nonland card name.\\nActivated abilities of sources with the chosen name can't be activated.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nDraw three cards.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may have Cryptoplasm become a copy of another target creature, except it has this ability.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, you may look at the top card of your library. You may cast it without paying its mana cost if it's an instant or sorcery spell.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may put a charge counter on target artifact.', 'Attacking creatures get +1/+0 and gain first strike until end of turn.', 'Battle cry (Whenever this creature attacks, each other attacking creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.)', 'Battle cry (Whenever this creature attacks, each other attacking creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.)\\nKuldotha Ringleader attacks each combat if able.', "Battle cry (Whenever this creature attacks, each other attacking creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.)\\nSignal Pest can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.", 'Battle cry (Whenever this creature attacks, each other attacking creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.)\\nWhenever Hero of Bladehold attacks, create two 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens that are tapped and attacking.', "Burn the Impure deals 3 damage to target creature. If that creature has infect, Burn the Impure deals 3 damage to that creature's controller.", "Choose one —\\n• Counter target artifact spell.\\n• Return target artifact to its owner's hand.", 'Choose one —\\n• Slagstorm deals 3 damage to each creature.\\n• Slagstorm deals 3 damage to each player.', "Concussive Bolt deals 4 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\nMetalcraft — If you control three or more artifacts, creatures controlled by that player or by that planeswalker's controller can't block this turn.", 'Counter target spell, then proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', "Create X 2/2 white Cat creature tokens. Shuffle White Sun's Zenith into its owner's library.", 'Create two 1/1 colorless Myr artifact creature tokens.', 'Creatures your opponents control get -2/-0 until end of turn.', "Defender\\nMetalcraft — As long as you control three or more artifacts, Spire Serpent gets +2/+2 and can attack as though it didn't have defender.", 'Destroy all artifacts.', 'Destroy all creatures, then create an X/X colorless Phyrexian Horror artifact creature token, where X is the number of creatures destroyed this way.', 'Destroy target artifact. You gain life equal to its mana value.', 'Destroy target creature with flying. Its controller gets a poison counter.', 'Destroy target creature, then proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', 'Destroy target nonartifact creature.', 'Destroy target noncreature artifact.', 'Double strike, protection from black and from green', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has infect. (It deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)', 'Enchant creature\\nYou control enchanted creature.\\nEnchanted creature has infect. (It deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)', 'Equipped creature gets +1/+0 and has first strike.\\nEquip {1}', 'Equipped creature gets +1/+1 and is an artifact in addition to its other types.\\nEquip {2}', "Equipped creature gets +2/+2 and can't block.\\nEquip {3} ({3}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", 'Equipped creature gets +2/+2 and has protection from black and from green.\\nWhenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, that player discards a card and you untap all lands you control.\\nEquip {2}', 'Exile two target artifacts.', 'First strike, deathtouch\\nWhenever a creature an opponent controls dies, you may return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'First strike, protection from red and from white\\nInfect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)', 'Flash\\nYou may cast artifact spells as though they had flash.', 'Flying', 'Flying, haste\\n{1}{R}: Hellkite Igniter gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is the number of artifacts you control.', "Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if you control no Thopters other than Thopter Assembly, return Thopter Assembly to its owner's hand and create five 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature tokens with flying.", 'Flying\\nInfect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)', 'Flying\\nInfect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nSacrifice a creature: Flesh-Eater Imp gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhen Serum Raker dies, each player discards a card.', "Flying\\nWhenever Victory's Herald attacks, attacking creatures gain flying and lifelink until end of turn.", 'Flying\\nWhenever a creature an opponent controls dies, you may gain 3 life.\\nWhenever an opponent discards a card, you may gain 3 life.', 'Flying\\nWhenever an opponent draws a card, you may draw two cards.', 'Flying\\nWhenever you cast an artifact spell, you may untap target creature.', "Forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Gain control of target artifact until end of turn. Untap that artifact. It gains haste until end of turn.', "Haste\\nBattle cry (Whenever this creature attacks, each other attacking creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.)\\nWhenever Hero of Oxid Ridge attacks, creatures with power 1 or less can't block this turn.", 'Imprint — When Knowledge Pool enters the battlefield, each player exiles the top three cards of their library.\\nWhenever a player casts a spell from their hand, that player exiles it. If the player does, they may cast a spell from among other cards exiled with Knowledge Pool without paying its mana cost.', 'Imprint — {T}: Exile target artifact card from a graveyard.\\nMyr Welder has all activated abilities of all cards exiled with it.', 'Indestructible\\nEquipped creature has indestructible.\\nEquip {2}', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you get a poison counter.', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nIf damage would be dealt to Phyrexian Hydra, prevent that damage. Put a -1/-1 counter on Phyrexian Hydra for each 1 damage prevented this way.', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nLifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nPhyrexian Juggernaut attacks each combat if able.', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nWhen Core Prowler dies, proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nWhen Viridian Corrupter enters the battlefield, destroy target artifact.', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nWhenever Septic Rats attacks, if defending player is poisoned, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Rot Wolf this turn dies, you may draw a card.', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'Living weapon (When this Equipment enters the battlefield, create a 0/0 black Phyrexian Germ creature token, then attach this to it.)\\nEquipped creature gets +0/+1 and has "Sacrifice this creature: This creature deals 1 damage to any target."\\nEquip {2}', 'Living weapon (When this Equipment enters the battlefield, create a 0/0 black Phyrexian Germ creature token, then attach this to it.)\\nEquipped creature gets +1/+1.\\nEquip {2}', 'Living weapon (When this Equipment enters the battlefield, create a 0/0 black Phyrexian Germ creature token, then attach this to it.)\\nEquipped creature gets +2/+2 and has flying.\\nEquip {6}', 'Living weapon (When this Equipment enters the battlefield, create a 0/0 black Phyrexian Germ creature token, then attach this to it.)\\nEquipped creature gets +2/+4 and has reach.\\nEquip {4}', 'Living weapon (When this Equipment enters the battlefield, create a 0/0 black Phyrexian Germ creature token, then attach this to it.)\\nEquipped creature gets +X/+X, where X is the number of creature cards in all graveyards.\\nEquip {2}', 'Look at the top five cards of your library. You may reveal any number of creature cards from among them and put the revealed cards into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', 'Look at the top seven cards of your library. You may put one of those cards onto the battlefield if it has the same name as a permanent. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', "Melira's Keepers can't have counters put on it.", 'Metalcraft — Ardent Recruit gets +2/+2 as long as you control three or more artifacts.', 'Metalcraft — Razorfield Rhino gets +2/+2 as long as you control three or more artifacts.', 'Metalcraft — Spiraling Duelist has double strike as long as you control three or more artifacts.', "Mountainwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", "Psychosis Crawler's power and toughness are each equal to the number of cards in your hand.\\nWhenever you draw a card, each opponent loses 1 life.", "Put X -1/-1 counters on each creature. Shuffle Black Sun's Zenith into its owner's library.", 'Put a -1/-1 counter on each attacking creature.', 'Put a -1/-1 counter on target creature. When that creature dies this turn, its controller gets a poison counter.', 'Put any number of target artifact cards from your graveyard on top of your library.\\nDraw a card.', "Put target artifact, creature, or enchantment on top of its owner's library.", "Put target creature card from an opponent's graveyard onto the battlefield under your control. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step. If that creature would leave the battlefield, exile it instead of putting it anywhere else.", 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nInfect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)', "Red Sun's Zenith deals X damage to any target. If a creature dealt damage this way would die this turn, exile it instead. Shuffle Red Sun's Zenith into its owner's library.", "Return all cards from your graveyard to your hand. Exile Praetor's Counsel. You have no maximum hand size for the rest of the game.", 'Return up to two target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return up to two target nonland permanents to their owners' hands.", "Sacrifice Gore Vassal: Put a -1/-1 counter on target creature. Then if that creature's toughness is 1 or greater, regenerate it.", 'Sacrifice an artifact: Gnathosaur gains trample until end of turn.', 'Sacrifice an artifact: Regenerate Rusted Slasher.', 'Search your library for a card, exile it, then shuffle. Any opponent may have you put that card into your hand. If no player does, you draw three cards.', "Search your library for a green creature card with mana value X or less, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle. Shuffle Green Sun's Zenith into its owner's library.", 'Shriekhorn enters the battlefield with three charge counters on it.\\n{T}, Remove a charge counter from Shriekhorn: Target player mills two cards.', "Shroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\nWhenever Neurok Commando deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card.", 'Sphere of the Suns enters the battlefield tapped and with three charge counters on it.\\n{T}, Remove a charge counter from Sphere of the Suns: Add one mana of any color.', 'Target creature gets +1/+1 and gains trample until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\\nMetalcraft — That creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn instead if you control three or more artifacts.', 'Target player discards a card, then mills a card.', "Target player draws X cards. Shuffle Blue Sun's Zenith into its owner's library.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nHexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\n{1}{G}: Regenerate Thrun, the Last Troll.", "Training Drone can't attack or block unless it's equipped.", 'Trample', "Trample, infect, indestructible\\nIf Blightsteel Colossus would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, reveal Blightsteel Colossus and shuffle it into its owner's library instead.", 'Vigilance\\nInfect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)', "Vigilance\\nKemba's Legion can block an additional creature each combat for each Equipment attached to Kemba's Legion.", 'When Blisterstick Shaman enters the battlefield, it deals 1 damage to any target.', 'When Caustic Hound dies, each player loses 4 life.', 'When Ichor Wellspring enters the battlefield or is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Kuldotha Flamefiend enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice an artifact. If you do, Kuldotha Flamefiend deals 4 damage divided as you choose among any number of targets.', "When Leonin Relic-Warder enters the battlefield, you may exile target artifact or enchantment.\\nWhen Leonin Relic-Warder leaves the battlefield, return the exiled card to the battlefield under its owner's control.", 'When Massacre Wurm enters the battlefield, creatures your opponents control get -2/-2 until end of turn.\\nWhenever a creature an opponent controls dies, that player loses 2 life.', 'When Myr Sire dies, create a 1/1 colorless Phyrexian Myr artifact creature token.', 'When Oculus dies, you may draw a card.', 'When Peace Strider enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.', 'When Phyrexian Rager enters the battlefield, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.', 'When Pierce Strider enters the battlefield, target opponent loses 3 life.', 'When Piston Sledge enters the battlefield, attach it to target creature you control.\\nEquipped creature gets +3/+1.\\nEquip—Sacrifice an artifact.', "When Spine of Ish Sah enters the battlefield, destroy target permanent.\\nWhen Spine of Ish Sah is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, return Spine of Ish Sah to its owner's hand.", 'When Treasure Mage enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an artifact card with mana value 6 or greater, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Viridian Emissary dies, you may search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "Whenever a creature deals combat damage to you, that creature's controller gains control of Contested War Zone.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Attacking creatures get +1/+0 until end of turn.", 'Whenever a source deals damage to Nested Ghoul, create a 2/2 black Phyrexian Zombie creature token.', 'Whenever an artifact is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, you may gain 5 life.', "Whenever another artifact is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, Magnetic Mine deals 2 damage to that artifact's controller.", "Whenever another nontoken artifact enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {2}. If you do, create a token that's a copy of that artifact.", '[+1]: Look at the top five cards of your library. You may reveal an artifact card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.\\n[−1]: Target artifact becomes an artifact creature with base power and toughness 5/5.\\n[−4]: Target player loses X life and you gain X life, where X is twice the number of artifacts you control.', '{2}{B}: Dross Ripper gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{2}{G}: Regenerate Tangle Hulk.', '{2}{U}, {T}: Put a -1/-1 counter on target creature. You may tap or untap that creature.', '{3}, {T}: Put a charge counter on Titan Forge.\\n{T}, Remove three charge counters from Titan Forge: Create a 9/9 colorless Golem artifact creature token.', '{4}, {T}: Target opponent loses 2 life, gets a poison counter, then mills six cards.', "{R}: Target creature can't block Spin Engine this turn.", '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}: Inkmoth Nexus becomes a 1/1 Phyrexian Blinkmoth artifact creature with flying and infect until end of turn. It's still a land. (It deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)", '{T}: Attach target Equipment you control to target creature you control.', '{T}: Create a 1/1 colorless Myr artifact creature token.\\n{T}, Tap five untapped Myr you control: Search your library for a Myr creature card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{U}: Gust-Skimmer gains flying until end of turn.', '{W}: Bladed Sentinel gains vigilance until end of turn.']
flavor: ['"A true Phyrexian predator. It will never know death, just as nature intended."\\n—Vorinclex, Voice of Hunger', '"A true warrior fights with whatever\'s handy."\\n—Qerk of the Secret Warren', '"All plans begin as dreams. I intend to awaken them."', '"All will be reforged in the fires of glory."\\n—Urabrask the Hidden', '"Anything that watches without sleep and fights without fear is a valuable ally against the Phyrexians."\\n—Kara Vrist, Neurok agent', '"As long as we have the will to fight, we are never without weapons."\\n—Koth of the Hammer', '"Domination by the strongest—that is all that matters in the Tangle now."\\n—Vorinclex, Voice of Hunger', '"Drive them back! Make their underworld into their grave!"\\n—Koth of the Hammer', '"Even a nuisance such as the pistus fly has a purpose in our new world."\\n—Glissa', '"Fall to your knees and welcome our embrace."\\n—Qal-Sha, Priest of Norn', '"I admire it. Few pull off pluck and subservience at the same time."\\n—Ezuri, renegade leader', '"I believe many worlds will bow to Phyrexia. Mirrodin is merely the first."\\n—Sheoldred, Whispering One', '"I fight for the suns, the surface, and everything in between."', '"I never move the same way twice. Those rotters can\'t grasp chaos."', '"If left in the enemy\'s shape too long, it might be lost to them."\\n—Vy Covalt, Neurok agent', '"If that brain can\'t figure out the secret of the serum, then add more brains."\\n—Rhmir, Hand of the Augur', '"If there can be no victory, then I will fight forever."\\n—Koth of the Hammer', '"In its gaze I saw no mercy, no recognition that I was worthy to exist."\\n—Kara Vrist, Neurok agent', '"It will be battle-ready before our strike at Oxid Ridge, and it will guarantee our victory."\\n—Ketuc of the Helm', '"It\'s a beautiful vision. Discarded debris is reborn as a singular entity."\\n—Urabrask the Hidden', '"Let their mindless armies come and face the might of genius."\\n—Varil, Neurok partisan', '"May our blessings sever the tongues of the forsaken."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"Our cause will ripen in the fertile flesh of the unworthy."\\n—Sheoldred, Whispering One', '"Our glorious infection has taken hold."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"Our land will not yield to Phyrexian corruption!"', '"Ours is a glorious transmission! Behold a future where all bow to the Father of Machines."\\n—Isila, Priest of Sheoldred', '"Pain isn\'t a negative stimulus. Pain is a sign of your imperfection."\\n—Sheoldred, Whispering One', '"Perfection is at hand. You have been freed of weakness and made *compleat*."\\n—Sheoldred, Whispering One', '"Phyrexians are tenacious. That\'s not the same thing as clever."\\n—Tezzeret', '"Phyrexians can\'t corrupt what they can\'t get close enough to touch."', '"Rid them of their unfaithful organs. Bring new hearts to the unbelievers."\\n—*Tome of Machines*, verse 1703', '"So, the survivors from Oxid Ridge are on the move. Let them come and witness predation in its purest form."\\n—Glissa', '"Specimen 211 examination report. Observation: graft sublimation incomplete. Result: death. Prepare specimen 212."', '"Such a creation serves no purpose other than exterminating every one of us."\\n—Sadra Alic, Neurok strategist', '"The Origin Query will wait. We must ensure we survive to return to it."\\n—Pelyus, vedalken ordinar', '"The Phyrexians *are* vulnerable. Do not despair. We will prevail!"\\n—Juryan, rebel leader', '"The Vanished must have sent it from beyond to aid us in this struggle."\\n—Kessla, Sylvok shaman', '"The chest cavity is cleared of useless meat. I know just what to do with the space."\\n—Gyed, Vault Priest', '"The fangren fight without comfort of any kind. We can ask no less of ourselves."\\n—Tilien, Sylvok partisan', '"The fleeting shadows of his primitive self have all but vanished."\\n—Jin-Gitaxias, Core Augur', '"The infection has spread farther than we could glimpse from the heights of Taj-Nar."', '"The union of the oil and necrogen has produced many pleasing reactions."\\n—Sheoldred, Whispering One', '"There\'s no more time for secluded study. Answers are there only for those with the courage to take them."', '"They believe they\'re driving us back, but we\'re leading them to their doom."\\n—Kethek, furnace stoker', '"They can\'t even comprehend nature. How could they improve it?"\\n—Venser', '"This war is not about loxodon or leonin, Sylvok or Auriok. To defeat these rotters, we must do it together."', '"Under the suns, Mirrodin kneels and begs us for perfection."\\n—Geth, Lord of the Vault', '"Unworthy of consecration."\\n—Axsh, lesser cenobite', '"Use everything. Iron, rust, scrap . . . even the ground must join our cause."\\n—Ezuri, renegade leader', '"Vulshok flail, Viridian shield, loxodon blade . . . Tazzir, bring the Moriok hook and assemble the rookies."\\n—Vy Covalt, Neurok agent', '"We lost our homes and our kin. We won\'t let those rotters take our future as well."', '"We will fight as they do: our flesh protected behind metal."\\n—Tae Aquil, Viridian weaponsmith', '"We will mourn when there is time. For now, we survive."', '"We will reveal the futility of their heresy by showing them how fragile their relics are."\\n—Vorinclex, Voice of Hunger', '"You are hopelessly obsolete, my brothers. Come and join the Great Work."\\n—Rhmir, Hand of the Augur', '"Your ideas will be discarded and your will repurposed."', "A golem's hands know no tenderness.", 'A mirror to draw its eye, a rod to rouse its rage, and a sword to break its bonds.', 'A new bird of prey—one that hunts sentience.', 'A productive warren requires a good deal of prodding.', 'A symbol of what Mirrodin once was and hope for what it will be again.', 'Accurate information is a precious commodity in times of war.', 'Adapted to tread on razorgrass, the rhino proved adept at treading on Phyrexians as well.', 'After the Battle of Liet Field, the white sun crested above Taj-Nar, bringing hope to all who survived the carnage.', 'As long as one drop of the oil exists, the joyous work continues.', "As the Phyrexian contagion corroded Karn's body, the praetors whispered psalms to corrupt his mind.", 'As the green sun crowned, Phyrexian prophecies glowed on the Tree of Tales.', 'At first, the Mirrans aimed for its exposed gut. The survivors quickly learned to do otherwise.', 'Basic senses like sight and taste are reserved for those in power.', "Being surrounded by goblins is less objectionable when they're fighting *for* you.", 'Blessed by the hands of Jin-Gitaxias.', 'Even the dead are raw materials for the Phyrexian vision of perfection.', "Flame doesn't kneel to Phyrexia.", 'For the Phyrexians, death is not an end, nor a one-time occurrence.', 'Having flesh is increasingly a liability on Mirrodin.', 'He didn\'t have a word for "home," but he knew it was something to be defended.', 'Her warriors are the last defense against the coming storm.', 'His crime was silence, and now he suffers it eternally.', "It chews open Mirrodin's husk and feeds on the outpouring of energy.", 'It evades Phyrexians by hiding in the spaces between seconds.', "It leaps from tree to tree, revealing the enemy's positions.", 'Its flight sets the sky itself on fire.', "Karn's creation is now his master.", 'Koth sent partisans into the Tangle to bring survivors to the safe haven of the tunnels below Kuldotha.', 'Life is ephemeral. Phyrexia is eternal.', 'Memnarch designed some myr to follow the levelers and reaffix lost parts. Mirran partisans put that instinct to good use.', 'Mirran creatures that could withstand the Phyrexian oil found an abundance of crunchy snacks.', 'Mycosynth grew unfettered beneath the black lacuna, metastasizing into a matrix of noxious energy.', 'Only the goblins could make a simple machine so complex.', 'Partisan spies warned that no armor would protect the body from Phyrexian infection. Neurok strategists took that as a challenge.', "Phyrexia's spiral of consumption grows ever wider and darker.", "Phyrexian smog clouds choked the skies, threatening creatures who couldn't comprehend the menace below.", 'Phyrexians research with the grace of surgeons and the finesse of butchers.', 'Sadly, the extent of Gerkk\'s healing knowledge was "don\'t pick at it."', 'Shock one, awe the rest.', 'The Mirran partisans created hundreds of patrol sentinels to divert Phyrexian assaults from the Tangle.', 'The corruption stirred the heavens above, awaking a shining champion.', "The faces of Geth's corpse-dredgers are disturbingly similar.", "The fiercest hunters in the Tangle don't seek out the mantises. They *are* the mantises.", 'The need to obey was inscribed on every plate in their bodies.', 'The serum from the blinkmoths they gather greases the joints of witch engines.', 'The squabble over succession was quickly replaced by the struggle to survive.', 'They watch for a new master, one more sinister than the last.', "Vorinclex removed its teeth so it wouldn't waste time chewing before moving to the next kill.", 'Where nature impedes, Phyrexians overcome.']
artist: ['Adrian Smith', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Austin Hsu', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Cos Koniotis', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Dave Allsop', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Rapoza', 'Efrem Palacios', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Erica Yang', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Greg Staples', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'Jana Schirmer & Johannes Voss', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kekai Kotaki', 'Kev Walker', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Marc Simonetti', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Mike Bierek', 'Nic Klein', 'Nils Hamm', 'Pete Venters', 'Randis Albion', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Scott Chou', 'Shelly Wan', 'Stephan Martiniere', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Whit Brachna', 'rk post']
